# Build trees
build/
build-*/
cmake-build-*/
CMakeUserPresets.json

# Compiled objects and binaries
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.so
*.so.*
*.dylib
*.dll
*.exe

# Sweep output. Everything under experiments/results is generated except the
# committed canonical summary and the per session manifests, which the report
# and CI build from. The session_manifest.json negation is kept for now because
# that file is tracked today and dropping the negation would leave it tracked
# and ignored at once; Phase A8a retires the file and removes the line then.
# archive/ needs two lines rather than one because git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so the directory itself has to be re included before any
# negation of a path inside it can take effect.
experiments/results/*
!experiments/results/.gitkeep
!experiments/results/summary.csv
!experiments/results/session_manifest.json
!experiments/results/archive/
!experiments/results/archive/**
!experiments/results/manifest-*.json

# Report intermediates. The published PDFs live under assets/reports/ and are
# tracked; everything LaTeX generates on the way there is not.
report/build/
report_debug/build/
*.aux
*.bbl
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.toc
*.lof
*.lot
*.synctex.gz
*.run.xml
*.bcf
report/main.pdf
report_debug/debug_report.pdf

# Generated report figures and tables. Regenerated from summary.csv by
# scripts/gen_report_assets.py, so they are outputs rather than sources.
report/figures/*.pdf
report/figures/*.png
report/tables/*.tex

# Private working material, kept locally and deliberately not published. The
# build specifications, CLAUDE.md, BOARD.md, tasks/ and .claude/ are
# instructions to the agent that built this project and the working files that
# schedule and track that work. They are not project documentation, they say
# nothing a reader of the library needs, and one `git add -A` would publish
# them, so they are ignored here rather than left to anyone's care. The
# specification pattern is unanchored so it covers the root copy and the docs
# copy alike. .claude/ used to be covered only by .git/info/exclude, which does
# not travel with a clone.
report_for_me/
BUILD_SPECIFICATION.md
CLAUDE.md
Parallel Numerical library V2.md
BOARD.md
tasks/
.claude/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Editor, tooling and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
